---
interface Props { source:'public'|'mls'; verifiedDemo?:boolean }
const {source}=Astro.props;
---
<section class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">REQUEST A VIEWING</p><h1>A little closer<br />to <em>feeling at home.</em></h1><p>Your email is verified. Save your details, then request a time from the shared calendar.</p><a href="/viewings/status/">My requests and verified account →</a></section>
<div class="portal-grid" id="intake" data-source={source}>
<aside class="card journey"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR VISIT, STEP BY STEP</p><ol><li>Verify your email</li><li>Save your visitor or agent details</li><li>Choose an available time</li><li>Submit a request for owner approval</li></ol><p>Submitting holds the slot, but the visit is not approved until an owner reviews it. One upcoming request or approved visit per verified email.</p><p class="hint">Identity, license and business-contact checks are simulated. No ID images are collected and no access codes are issued. The MLS entry route is not proof of agent identity.</p></aside>
<section class="card"><h2 id="intake-title">Tell us about your visit.</h2><p>Your details and requests are saved to your verified account and are visible to owners.</p>
<form id="intake-form"><fieldset id="profile-fields" disabled><legend>Visitor details</legend><label for="visitor-name">Your name</label><input id="visitor-name" autocomplete="name" maxlength="120" required />
<label for="visitor-role">Are you a licensed real-estate agent?</label><select id="visitor-role"><option value="buyer">No — prospective buyer</option><option value="agent" selected={source==='mls'}>Yes — real-estate agent</option></select>
<fieldset id="agent-fields" hidden><legend>Agent details · provided by you</legend><label for="agent-name">Licensed name</label><input id="agent-name" maxlength="120" /><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="license-state">Issuing state or jurisdiction</label><input id="license-state" maxlength="80" /></div><div><label for="license-number">License number</label><input id="license-number" maxlength="80" /></div></div><label for="brokerage">Brokerage</label><input id="brokerage" maxlength="160" /><p class="hint">Your verified email is your contact address. License and business-contact validation will be recorded as a simulated pass, not real verification.</p></fieldset>
<p class="inset" id="verification-explanation">Identity validation is simulated. Saving your profile lets you request a time; it does not prove identity or authorize entry.</p><button class="button" type="submit">Save details and continue →</button></fieldset><p id="profile-result" role="status">Loading your saved profile…</p><button class="text-button" id="reload-profile" type="button">Reload saved profile</button></form>
<section id="slot-step" hidden><p class="badge" id="verification-badge"></p><h2>Choose an available time.</h2><p>Shared calendar · America/New_York. Selecting a time does not hold it. Submitting a request holds it pending owner approval.</p><h3 id="calendar-heading">Rolling availability</h3><p id="calendar-range"></p><div class="calendar-grid" id="visitor-calendar" role="group" aria-label="Available viewing days"></div><h3 id="selected-day"></h3><div class="slot-tiles" id="slot-list" role="group" aria-label="Available viewing times"></div><p id="slot-empty" role="status"></p>
<label class="check" id="attending-wrap" hidden><input id="agent-attending" type="checkbox" /> I will attend the showing and will not share access for an unaccompanied buyer visit.</label>
<button class="button" id="review-request" type="button" disabled>Review request</button><section id="booking-review" class="inset" hidden><h3>Review your request</h3><p id="review-summary"></p><button class="button" id="confirm-booking" type="button">Submit request and hold this time</button></section><p id="request-result" role="status" tabindex="-1"></p><a href="/viewings/status/">View my saved requests →</a><br /><button class="text-button" id="restart" type="button">← Edit my details</button></section>
</section></div><script>import '../scripts/viewing-intake';</script>
